# Wired Cursor discovery (gitignore)

**Skill:** `.cursor/skills/author-ai-copilots/SKILL.md` (three Cursor skill sources).

## MUST

- Treat **pack** symlinks from `link-into-project.sh` as **committed** (pin is `.cursor/packs/shared` gitlink only).
- Treat **Go-module** and other **fire-and-forget** wires under `.cursor/skills/` or `.cursor/rules/` as **gitignored** (symlink may point at module cache).
- When adding or renaming a BOOTSTRAP `ln` or `make wire-cursor-skills` target for such a path, append the repo-relative path to `.cursor/wired-gitignore.manifest`.
- Run `.cursor/packs/shared/scripts/sync-wired-cursor-gitignore.sh --project .` in the same change (or before commit).
- Load `install-repo-hooks` on new clones; wire + sync keeps `git status` clean.

## MUST NOT

- Commit Go-module wired symlinks to satisfy `??` in `git status`.
- Hand-edit lines between the `BEGIN` / `END cursor-packs wired Cursor discovery` markers in `.gitignore` (run the sync script instead).
- Add product-only library rules to cursor-packs to avoid host gitignore (use manifest + sync).

## Enforcement

Before claiming a wire change is done: manifest lists the path; sync script exit 0; `git status` does not show the wired path as untracked (unless intentionally not wired yet).
